      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ae5c147906bfd12e600dc47|full_name}: It's non-trivial to determine exactly which shader broke things, and randomly replacing all shaders with fallbacks is a great way to make a world completely unusable.\n\nAlso, usually the bad shaders are not widespread (because they're terrible in VR and anyone who is testing in VR realizes this and fixes them or uses a different shader). So a global blacklist is probably not too useful.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
